  Opened by the open button of Assembly in the Quick Draw window (it closes with 5, the Lisp
  shows this one: Dyl:QuickDrawAsmDialog of Apps\Draw\Dyl-QuickDraw.lsp), on the assembly of
  the preset shown. A preset window (Installer\Windows\Engine\Presets.cs): its list "lst" is
  the assembly presets (pst/rows: id group name layers border-lines dividing-lines exterior
  units description load-bearing-rating non-load-bearing-rating stc iic family
  family-description, then the columns the Lisp adds: 15 the layers as rows, their thicknesses
  in the units of the drawing, 16 to 27 the Border lines, 28 to 39 the Dividing lines: on,
  layer key, the properties they override; the default assemblies, the typical assemblies of
  the building code, in pst/defs for Reset), listed by family (pst/family: B6 for B6a to B6e,
  its number of variants beside it). The family box holds what its variants share: its name
  (fam, 13), its group, its short description (fds, 14), its exterior and its lines (given to
  every variant, pst/famcols). The variant shown is picked in the list var at the top of the
  Layers box (its name and its ratings), New variant (vnw) adds a copy of it named with the
  next letter (B6f), Delete (vdl) deletes a custom variant; its name (nam, 2), its description
  and its ratings are under it. New and Copy add a family of one variant, Delete deletes the
  custom families selected; all of it runs in the window; OK saves them and gives the assembly selected to the Quick Draw presets
  selected. Border lines (abl, its two faces and its ends) and Dividing lines (adl, between
  its layers) are checkboxes of the preset (Lisp: wtiles), their open buttons the Border
  Settings window on their columns of the assemblies selected (Presets.cs: Win.Columns).
  Exterior (aex, column 6: "First" or "Last") says which end of the list of layers is the
  outside of the wall, for the low permeance ratio. What the assembly is worth by the building
  code (under its name, over its layers): its description (ads, 8), its fire-resistance ratings in
  minutes (afl load-bearing, 9; afn non-load-bearing, 10), its STC (ast, 11) and its IIC (aii,
  12), each empty when it is not known.
  The layers of the assembly shown are a list of rows edited in the window (Rows.cs), held in
  the column 15 of the assembly (dyl:Win.RowsIn), greyed out while several assemblies are
  selected (pst.many): a row per layer, its columns: 0 the kind ("P"), 1 its material (its
  id; the Material list shows the materials of the group of its Group list, 43:
  dyl:Win.ListBy, lp/by the group of each material), 2 its thickness, 3 the layer key of its
  hatch ("": the hatch layer key of its material), 4 not used;
  5 its own band settings on ("1"), 6 to 13 those settings (hatch aligned to,
  ends, extension, angle, corners, miter limit, lap, joints: edited in the Band Settings
  window, opened by lbe on the layers selected), 14 its own border on, 15 the layer key of
  that border (edited in the Border Settings window, opened by lbo on the layers selected,
  with the properties it overrides in 17 to 26: color on, color, linetype on, linetype,
  linetype scale on, scale, lineweight on, lineweight, transparency on, transparency), 16
  Load-bearing ("1", lsr: any number of layers; the Justification Load-bearing layers of a
  Quick Draw preset puts the line drawn in the middle of all of them together), 27 Has a hatch ("0": no hatch, the outline only), 28 to 37
  the properties its hatch overrides (as its border; edited with its layer key, column 3, in
  the Hatch Settings window, opened by lho on the layers selected), 38 to 42 the scale and the
  origin of its hatch, with its band settings (scale by width, width factor, origin on line,
  origin X, origin Y), 43 the group of its material (read, never saved), 44 the material of
  its framing ("" None, lfm: a discontinuous layer, the studs and the insulation between
  them, the material of the layer), 45 the share of its area in percent (lfp), 46 Variable
  thickness (lvt) and 47 Low permeance (llp, one at most: dyl:Win.Exclusive="lock", greyed out in the
  other rows while one has it, Free[47] in the list), the three checkboxes also checked in
  the list (Win.Toggle, small boxes: Dyl.Check).
  Each row shows the thermal resistance and the mass of its layer (P[1:2:lp/rsi:44:45:lfm/rsi:p],
  P[1:2:lp/mass:44:45:lfm/mass:a], Rows.cs), from the data of its material, of its framing
  and its thickness, a dash when it has none: the framing and the insulation in parallel for
  the resistance (the isothermal planes method of the building code), by their areas for the
  mass. Under the list, ltm
  (metric) and lti (imperial, mt.imp) add up the thermal resistance and the mass of the layers
  from lp/rsi and lp/mass, the data of each material (Remote>>Dyl:MaterialDataLists). Add, Remove,
  Move up, Move down and Flip run in the window. The preview (an AssemblyTile,
  Installer\Windows\Engine\Assembly.cs) draws the rows as they are edited: lp/specs the
  preview of each material (scaled by the thickness of a layer whose band settings say so), ll/ends the ends of the whole band, ll/paper the inches of a drawing
  unit and the drawing scale.
-->
<Window xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        xmlns:dyl="clr-namespace:DynALisp.Windows"
        Title="DynALisp - Assembly Presets" dyl:Win.Docs="Draw\Dyl-AssemblyPresets.htm">
  <Window.Resources>
    <Style x:Key="Row" TargetType="DockPanel">
      <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,3"/>
      <Setter Property="LastChildFill" Value="True"/>
    </Style>
  </Window.Resources>
  <!-- Its columns get narrower down to their MinWidth when the window is (Engine\Fit.cs), the
       column of the layer on the right as it is: -->
  <Grid Margin="14">
    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
      <ColumnDefinition Width="370" MinWidth="300"/>
      <ColumnDefinition Width="10"/>
      <ColumnDefinition Width="640" MinWidth="540"/>
      <ColumnDefinition Width="10"/>
      <ColumnDefinition Width="330" MinWidth="280"/>
    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
    <Grid.RowDefinitions>
      <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
      <RowDefinition Height="*"/>
      <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
      <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
    </Grid.RowDefinitions>

    <!-- The assemblies (Ctrl / Shift click: several edited at once): -->
    <GroupBox Grid.RowSpan="2" Header="Assemblies" Margin="0">
      <DockPanel>
        <DockPanel DockPanel.Dock="Top" Margin="0,0,0,8">
          <ComboBox x:Name="srt" DockPanel.Dock="Right" Width="90" Margin="8,0,0,0" ToolTip="Sort by"/>
          <TextBox x:Name="flt" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Search}" Tag="Filter" MaxLength="64"/>
        </DockPanel>
        <DockPanel DockPanel.Dock="Top" Margin="0,0,0,10">
          <TextBlock DockPanel.Dock="Left" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Label}" Text="Show"/>
          <Button x:Name="shd" DockPanel.Dock="Right" Content="Set default"/>
          <ComboBox x:Name="shg"/>
        </DockPanel>
        <Grid DockPanel.Dock="Top" Margin="6,0,10,4">
          <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="86"/>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
          </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
          <TextBlock Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Sub}" Margin="0" Text="Group"/>
          <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Sub}" Margin="0" Text="Family"/>
          <TextBlock x:Name="pcn" Grid.Column="1" HorizontalAlignment="Right" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" FontSize="11.5" Foreground="{DynamicResource Dyl.Muted}"/>
        </Grid>
        <!-- the buttons as wide as the column, narrower with it: -->
        <UniformGrid DockPanel.Dock="Bottom" Rows="1" Margin="0,10,0,0">
          <Button x:Name="new" Margin="0,0,4,0" MinWidth="0" Content="New"/>
          <Button x:Name="cpy" Margin="4,0,4,0" MinWidth="0" Content="Copy"/>
          <Button x:Name="del" Margin="4,0,0,0" MinWidth="0" Content="Delete"/>
        </UniformGrid>
        <ListBox x:Name="lst" MinHeight="200">
          <ListBox.ItemTemplate>
            <DataTemplate>
              <Grid>
                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                  <ColumnDefinition Width="86"/>
                  <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                <TextBlock Foreground="{DynamicResource Dyl.Muted}" Text="{Binding Group}" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"/>
                <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding Name}" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" Margin="0,0,34,0"/>
                <!-- its number of variants: -->
                <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" HorizontalAlignment="Right" Foreground="{DynamicResource Dyl.Muted}" Text="{Binding Count}" ToolTip="Variants"/>
              </Grid>
            </DataTemplate>
          </ListBox.ItemTemplate>
        </ListBox>
      </DockPanel>
    </GroupBox>

    <!-- The family shown: its name, its group, its short description, its exterior and its
         lines, the same for all its variants (given to every variant of the families
         selected). Its boxes take the width of the column: -->
    <GroupBox Grid.Column="2" Padding="16,0,16,14" Margin="0">
        <Grid>
          <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="24"/>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="130"/>
          </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
          <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
          </Grid.RowDefinitions>
          <TextBlock Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Label}" Text="Family"/>
          <DockPanel Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource Row}">
            <TextBox x:Name="fam" MaxLength="64"/>
          </DockPanel>
          <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Label}" Text="Group"/>
          <DockPanel Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource Row}">
            <dyl:OpenButton x:Name="gre" DockPanel.Dock="Left" Margin="0,0,8,0" dyl:Win.Close="8" ToolTip="Preset Groups"/>
            <ComboBox x:Name="grp"/>
          </DockPanel>
          <!-- What its variants share, in a few words: -->
          <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Label}" Text="Description"/>
          <DockPanel Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="1" Grid.ColumnSpan="4" Style="{StaticResource Row}">
            <TextBox x:Name="fds" MaxLength="400"/>
          </DockPanel>
          <TextBlock x:Name="prm" Grid.Row="3" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Desc}" Margin="0,4,0,0" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
          <!-- The lines of the assembly, replaced by the own border of a layer: its two faces
               and its ends, then the lines between its layers (the Border Settings window on
               the assemblies selected): -->
          <DockPanel Grid.Column="3" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" Style="{StaticResource Row}">
            <dyl:OpenButton x:Name="abo" DockPanel.Dock="Right" ToolTip="Border Settings" dyl:Win.EnabledBy="abl"
                            dyl:Win.Open="Dyl-QuickDrawBorderSettings.xaml"
                            dyl:Win.Columns="out:17,bco:18,bcv:19,blo:20,blt:21,bso:22,bsc:23,bwo:24,bwt:25,bto:26,btr:27"/>
            <CheckBox x:Name="abl" Content="Border lines"/>
          </DockPanel>
          <DockPanel Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="3" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" Style="{StaticResource Row}">
            <dyl:OpenButton x:Name="ado" DockPanel.Dock="Right" ToolTip="Border Settings" dyl:Win.EnabledBy="adl"
                            dyl:Win.Open="Dyl-QuickDrawBorderSettings.xaml"
                            dyl:Win.Columns="out:29,bco:30,bcv:31,blo:32,blt:33,bso:34,bsc:35,bwo:36,bwt:37,bto:38,btr:39"/>
            <CheckBox x:Name="adl" Content="Dividing lines"/>
          </DockPanel>
          <!-- Which end of the layers is the outside (the low permeance ratio): -->
          <TextBlock Grid.Row="3" Grid.Column="3" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Label}" Text="Exterior"/>
          <DockPanel Grid.Row="3" Grid.Column="4" Style="{StaticResource Row}">
            <ComboBox x:Name="aex"/>
          </DockPanel>
        </Grid>
    </GroupBox>
    <GroupBox Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="2" Header="Layers" Margin="0,10,0,0" dyl:Win.EnabledBy="!pst.many">
      <DockPanel>
        <!-- The variant shown (its name and ratings in the list), a new one copied from it,
             its name, its description and what the building code gives it (Tables
             9.10.3.1.-A and -B for the default assemblies): its fire-resistance ratings in
             minutes and its sound classes, each empty when it is not known: -->
        <Grid DockPanel.Dock="Top" Margin="0,0,0,12">
          <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
          </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
          <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
          </Grid.RowDefinitions>
          <TextBlock Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Label}" Text="Variant"/>
          <DockPanel Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource Row}">
            <Button x:Name="vdl" DockPanel.Dock="Right" Content="Delete"/>
            <Button x:Name="vnw" DockPanel.Dock="Right" Margin="8,0,0,0" Content="New variant"/>
            <ComboBox x:Name="var"/>
          </DockPanel>
          <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Label}" Text="Name"/>
          <DockPanel Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource Row}">
            <TextBox x:Name="nam" MaxLength="64"/>
          </DockPanel>
          <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Label}" Text="Description"/>
          <DockPanel Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource Row}">
            <TextBox x:Name="ads" MaxLength="400"/>
          </DockPanel>
          <TextBlock Grid.Row="3" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Label}" Text="Fire, min"/>
          <StackPanel Grid.Row="3" Grid.Column="1" Orientation="Horizontal" Margin="0,3">
            <TextBlock Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Label}" Text="Load-bearing"/>
            <TextBox x:Name="afl" Width="70" MaxLength="4"
                     dyl:Win.Check="empty;integer;min=0" dyl:Win.CheckMessage="The fire-resistance ratings must be whole numbers of minutes."/>
            <TextBlock Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Label}" Margin="20,0,8,0" Text="Non-load-bearing"/>
            <TextBox x:Name="afn" Width="70" MaxLength="4"
                     dyl:Win.Check="empty;integer;min=0" dyl:Win.CheckMessage="The fire-resistance ratings must be whole numbers of minutes."/>
          </StackPanel>
          <TextBlock Grid.Row="4" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Label}" Text="Sound"/>
          <StackPanel Grid.Row="4" Grid.Column="1" Orientation="Horizontal" Margin="0,3">
            <TextBlock Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Label}" Text="STC"/>
            <TextBox x:Name="ast" Width="70" MaxLength="3"
                     dyl:Win.Check="empty;integer;min=0" dyl:Win.CheckMessage="The STC must be a whole number."/>
            <TextBlock Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Label}" Margin="20,0,8,0" Text="IIC"/>
            <TextBox x:Name="aii" Width="70" MaxLength="3"
                     dyl:Win.Check="empty;integer;min=0" dyl:Win.CheckMessage="The IIC must be a whole number."/>
          </StackPanel>
        </Grid>
        <Grid DockPanel.Dock="Top" Margin="6,0,10,4">
          <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="80"/>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="70"/>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="56"/>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="56"/>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="40"/>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="40"/>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="40"/>
          </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
          <TextBlock Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Sub}" Margin="0" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" Text="Group"/>
          <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Sub}" Margin="0" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" Text="Material"/>
          <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Sub}" Margin="0" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" HorizontalAlignment="Right" Text="Thickness"/>
          <!-- The thermal resistance and the mass per area of each layer (RSI and kg/m2 in a
               metric drawing, R and lb/ft2 in an imperial one, mt.imp): -->
          <TextBlock Grid.Column="3" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Sub}" Margin="0" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" HorizontalAlignment="Right" Text="RSI" dyl:Win.VisibleBy="!mt.imp"/>
          <TextBlock Grid.Column="3" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Sub}" Margin="0" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" HorizontalAlignment="Right" Text="R" dyl:Win.VisibleBy="mt.imp"/>
          <TextBlock Grid.Column="4" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Sub}" Margin="0" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" HorizontalAlignment="Right" Text="Mass"/>
          <!-- Load-bearing (16), Variable thickness (46) and Low permeance (47), checked in the
               list itself, by their abbreviations (their names in the legend under the list
               and in their tooltips): -->
          <TextBlock Grid.Column="5" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Sub}" Margin="0" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" HorizontalAlignment="Center" Text="LB" ToolTip="Load-bearing"/>
          <TextBlock Grid.Column="6" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Sub}" Margin="0" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" HorizontalAlignment="Center" Text="VT" ToolTip="Variable thickness"/>
          <TextBlock Grid.Column="7" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Sub}" Margin="0" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" HorizontalAlignment="Center" Text="LP" ToolTip="Low permeance"/>
        </Grid>
        <DockPanel DockPanel.Dock="Bottom" Margin="0,10,0,0">
          <Button x:Name="la" DockPanel.Dock="Left" Margin="0" Content="Add" dyl:Win.Do="add"/>
          <Button x:Name="ld" DockPanel.Dock="Left" Content="Remove" dyl:Win.Do="remove"/>
          <Button x:Name="lf" DockPanel.Dock="Right" Content="Flip" dyl:Win.Do="flip"/>
          <Button x:Name="lv" DockPanel.Dock="Right" Content="Move down" dyl:Win.Do="down"/>
          <Button x:Name="lu" DockPanel.Dock="Right" Content="Move up" dyl:Win.Do="up"/>
          <Border/>
        </DockPanel>
        <!-- The names of the abbreviated columns, at the bottom: -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="lab" DockPanel.Dock="Bottom" Foreground="{DynamicResource Dyl.Muted}" FontSize="11" Margin="6,8,0,0"
                   Text="LB  Load-bearing     VT  Variable thickness     LP  Low permeance"/>
        <!-- The thermal resistance of the continuous layers, those without a framing (over
             the thermal bridges of the framing), once a layer has one, and the low permeance
             ratio: the layers from
             the exterior (aex) to the one checked Low permeance, over the others: -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="lrf" DockPanel.Dock="Bottom" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Desc}" Margin="6,2,0,0" dyl:Win.VisibleBy="aex!=Last"
                   dyl:Win.Summary="{}{ratio:first:1:2:lp/rsi:44:45:lfm/rsi:p@llp|Low permeance ratio #|Low permeance ratio unknown}" dyl:Win.SummaryEmpty=""/>
        <TextBlock x:Name="lrl" DockPanel.Dock="Bottom" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Desc}" Margin="6,2,0,0" dyl:Win.VisibleBy="aex=Last"
                   dyl:Win.Summary="{}{ratio:last:1:2:lp/rsi:44:45:lfm/rsi:p@llp|Low permeance ratio #|Low permeance ratio unknown}" dyl:Win.SummaryEmpty=""/>
        <TextBlock x:Name="lcm" DockPanel.Dock="Bottom" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Desc}" Margin="6,2,0,0" dyl:Win.VisibleBy="!mt.imp"
                   dyl:Win.Summary="{}{over:1:2:lp/rsi:44:45:lfm/rsi:p@lfm=@lfm!=|Continuous layers # m²·K/W|Continuous layers unknown}" dyl:Win.SummaryEmpty=""/>
        <TextBlock x:Name="lcu" DockPanel.Dock="Bottom" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Desc}" Margin="6,2,0,0" dyl:Win.VisibleBy="mt.imp"
                   dyl:Win.Summary="{}{over:1:2:lp/rsi:44:45:lfm/rsi:p@lfm=@lfm!=|Continuous layers R #|Continuous layers unknown}" dyl:Win.SummaryEmpty=""/>
        <!-- Under the layers: their thermal resistance and their mass per area, added up from
             the data of their materials (lp/rsi, lp/mass), in the units of the drawing, the
             layers whose material has no such data counted apart: -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="ltm" DockPanel.Dock="Bottom" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Desc}" Margin="6,2,0,0" dyl:Win.VisibleBy="!mt.imp"
                   dyl:Win.Summary="Thermal resistance {per:1:2:lp/rsi:44:45:lfm/rsi:p} m²·K/W{miss:1:lp/rsi:44:45:lfm/rsi|, 1 layer unknown|, # layers unknown}  ·  Mass {per:1:2:lp/mass:44:45:lfm/mass:a} kg/m²{miss:1:lp/mass:44:45:lfm/mass|, 1 layer unknown|, # layers unknown}"
                   dyl:Win.SummaryEmpty=""/>
        <TextBlock x:Name="lti" DockPanel.Dock="Bottom" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Desc}" Margin="6,2,0,0" dyl:Win.VisibleBy="mt.imp"
                   dyl:Win.Summary="Thermal resistance R {per:1:2:lp/rsi:44:45:lfm/rsi:p}{miss:1:lp/rsi:44:45:lfm/rsi|, 1 layer unknown|, # layers unknown}  ·  Mass {per:1:2:lp/mass:44:45:lfm/mass:a} lb/ft²{miss:1:lp/mass:44:45:lfm/mass|, 1 layer unknown|, # layers unknown}"
                   dyl:Win.SummaryEmpty=""/>
        <TextBlock x:Name="lt" DockPanel.Dock="Bottom" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Desc}" Margin="6,8,0,0"
                   dyl:Win.Summary="{}{count:|layer|layers}, width {sum:2}"
                   dyl:Win.SummaryEmpty="No layers."/>
        <!-- Ctrl / Shift click: several layers edited at once: -->
        <ListBox x:Name="ll" MinHeight="200" dyl:Win.Rows="1" dyl:Win.RowsIn="15">
          <ListBox.ItemTemplate>
            <DataTemplate>
              <Grid>
                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                  <ColumnDefinition Width="80"/>
                  <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                  <ColumnDefinition Width="70"/>
                  <ColumnDefinition Width="56"/>
                  <ColumnDefinition Width="56"/>
                  <ColumnDefinition Width="40"/>
                  <ColumnDefinition Width="40"/>
                  <ColumnDefinition Width="40"/>
                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                <TextBlock Foreground="{DynamicResource Dyl.Muted}" Text="{Binding [43]}" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" Margin="0,0,8,0"/>
                <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Margin="0,0,8,0">
                  <TextBlock x:Name="pre" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis">
                    <Run Text="{Binding [1], Mode=OneWay}"/><Run x:Name="hk" Foreground="{DynamicResource Dyl.Muted}" Text="{Binding V[3], Mode=OneWay, StringFormat='{}  [{0}]'}"/><Run x:Name="fr" Text="{Binding [44], Mode=OneWay, StringFormat='{}  + {0}'}"/><Run x:Name="fp" Text="{Binding V[45], Mode=OneWay, StringFormat='{} {0}%'}"/>
                  </TextBlock>
                  <!-- Its own band settings (its ends, its corners) and its own border: -->
                  <TextBlock x:Name="own" Foreground="{DynamicResource Dyl.Muted}" FontSize="11" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis">
                    <Run x:Name="bd" Text="{Binding V[7], Mode=OneWay}"/><Run x:Name="bc" Text="{Binding V[10], Mode=OneWay, StringFormat='{}, {0}'}"/><Run x:Name="bk" Text="{Binding V[15], Mode=OneWay, StringFormat='{}  |  Border {0}'}"/>
                  </TextBlock>
                </StackPanel>
                <TextBlock x:Name="thk" Grid.Column="2" HorizontalAlignment="Right" Text="{Binding V[2]}"/>
                <!-- From the data of its material and its thickness (lp/rsi, lp/mass, as the
                     total under the list), a dash when its material has none: -->
                <TextBlock Grid.Column="3" HorizontalAlignment="Right" Text="{Binding P[1:2:lp/rsi:44:45:lfm/rsi:p|–]}"/>
                <TextBlock Grid.Column="4" HorizontalAlignment="Right" Text="{Binding P[1:2:lp/mass:44:45:lfm/mass:a|–]}"/>
                <CheckBox Grid.Column="5" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Check}" HorizontalAlignment="Center" ToolTip="Load-bearing" dyl:Win.Toggle="16"
                          IsChecked="{Binding V[16], Mode=OneWay, Converter={x:Static dyl:On.Converter}}"/>
                <CheckBox Grid.Column="6" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Check}" HorizontalAlignment="Center" ToolTip="Variable thickness" dyl:Win.Toggle="46"
                          IsChecked="{Binding V[46], Mode=OneWay, Converter={x:Static dyl:On.Converter}}"/>
                <CheckBox Grid.Column="7" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Check}" HorizontalAlignment="Center" ToolTip="Low permeance" dyl:Win.Toggle="47"
                          IsEnabled="{Binding Free[47]}"
                          IsChecked="{Binding V[47], Mode=OneWay, Converter={x:Static dyl:On.Converter}}"/>
              </Grid>
              <DataTemplate.Triggers>
                <DataTrigger Binding="{Binding V[5]}" Value="0">
                  <Setter TargetName="bd" Property="Text" Value=""/>
                  <Setter TargetName="bc" Property="Text" Value=""/>
                  <Setter TargetName="bk" Property="Text" Value="{Binding V[15], Mode=OneWay, StringFormat='Border {0}'}"/>
                </DataTrigger>
                <DataTrigger Binding="{Binding V[14]}" Value="0">
                  <Setter TargetName="bk" Property="Text" Value=""/>
                </DataTrigger>
                <MultiDataTrigger>
                  <MultiDataTrigger.Conditions>
                    <Condition Binding="{Binding V[5]}" Value="0"/>
                    <Condition Binding="{Binding V[14]}" Value="0"/>
                  </MultiDataTrigger.Conditions>
                  <Setter TargetName="own" Property="Visibility" Value="Collapsed"/>
                </MultiDataTrigger>
                <DataTrigger Binding="{Binding V[3]}" Value="">
                  <Setter TargetName="hk" Property="Text" Value=""/>
                </DataTrigger>
                <DataTrigger Binding="{Binding V[27]}" Value="0">
                  <Setter TargetName="hk" Property="Text" Value="  No hatch"/>
                </DataTrigger>
                <!-- Its framing (a discontinuous layer) and the share of its area: -->
                <DataTrigger Binding="{Binding V[44]}" Value="">
                  <Setter TargetName="fr" Property="Text" Value=""/>
                  <Setter TargetName="fp" Property="Text" Value=""/>
                </DataTrigger>
              </DataTemplate.Triggers>
            </DataTemplate>
          </ListBox.ItemTemplate>
        </ListBox>
      </DockPanel>
    </GroupBox>

    <DockPanel Grid.Column="4" Grid.RowSpan="2">
    <!-- The layer shown (the first one selected); with none selected, the layer Add adds: -->
    <GroupBox DockPanel.Dock="Top" Header="Parameters" Margin="0" dyl:Win.EnabledBy="!pst.many" dyl:Win.Summary="Parameters{sel| (# selected)}">
      <StackPanel>
        <!-- The group of its material (the materials of the Material list): -->
        <DockPanel Style="{StaticResource Row}">
          <TextBlock DockPanel.Dock="Left" Width="88" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Label}" Text="Group"/>
          <ComboBox x:Name="lg" dyl:Win.Column="43"/>
        </DockPanel>
        <DockPanel Style="{StaticResource Row}">
          <TextBlock DockPanel.Dock="Left" Width="88" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Label}" Text="Material"/>
          <ComboBox x:Name="lp" dyl:Win.Column="1" dyl:Win.ListBy="lg"/>
        </DockPanel>
        <DockPanel Style="{StaticResource Row}">
          <TextBlock DockPanel.Dock="Left" Width="88" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Label}" Text="Thickness"/>
          <TextBox x:Name="lw" dyl:Win.Column="2"
                   dyl:Win.Check="positive" dyl:Win.CheckMessage="The thickness must be a number greater than 0."/>
        </DockPanel>
        <!-- The structural layer, the line of the band on its middle (Structural layer): -->
        <DockPanel Style="{StaticResource Row}">
          <CheckBox x:Name="lsr" Content="Load-bearing" dyl:Win.Column="16"/>
        </DockPanel>
        <!-- A discontinuous layer: the material of its framing (the studs, "" None; the
             material of the layer is the insulation between them) and its share of the area: -->
        <DockPanel Style="{StaticResource Row}">
          <TextBlock DockPanel.Dock="Left" Width="88" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Label}" Text="Framing"/>
          <ComboBox x:Name="lfm" dyl:Win.Column="44"/>
        </DockPanel>
        <DockPanel Style="{StaticResource Row}" dyl:Win.EnabledBy="lfm!=">
          <TextBlock DockPanel.Dock="Left" Width="88" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Label}" Text="Framing %"/>
          <TextBox x:Name="lfp" dyl:Win.Column="45"
                   dyl:Win.Check="positive;max=99.9" dyl:Win.CheckMessage="The framing must be a percentage greater than 0 and less than 100."/>
        </DockPanel>
        <!-- What the layer is (also checked in the list): its thickness varies (a tapered
             insulation), a continuous insulation over the framing, the layer of low
             permeance (one at most): -->
        <DockPanel Style="{StaticResource Row}">
          <CheckBox x:Name="lvt" Content="Variable thickness" dyl:Win.Column="46"/>
        </DockPanel>
        <DockPanel Style="{StaticResource Row}">
          <CheckBox x:Name="llp" Content="Low permeance" dyl:Win.Column="47" dyl:Win.Exclusive="lock"/>
        </DockPanel>
        <!-- Its own band settings (the Band Settings window on the layers selected), its
             hatch and its own border, in place of the lines of the assembly (the Hatch
             Settings and Border Settings windows on the layers selected: their layer key and
             the properties they override): -->
        <DockPanel Style="{StaticResource Row}">
          <dyl:OpenButton x:Name="lbe" DockPanel.Dock="Right" ToolTip="Band Settings" dyl:Win.EnabledBy="lbs"
                          dyl:Win.Open="Dyl-QuickDrawBandSettings.xaml"
                          dyl:Win.Columns="mht:6,men:7,mex:8,mea:9,mco:10,mml:11,mlt:12,mjo:13,msw:38,mfc:39,mor:40,moa:41,mof:42"/>
          <CheckBox x:Name="lbs" Content="Custom band settings" dyl:Win.Column="5"/>
        </DockPanel>
        <DockPanel Style="{StaticResource Row}">
          <dyl:OpenButton x:Name="lho" DockPanel.Dock="Right" ToolTip="Hatch Settings" dyl:Win.EnabledBy="lha"
                          dyl:Win.Open="Dyl-QuickDrawHatchSettings.xaml"
                          dyl:Win.Columns="hky:3,bco:28,bcv:29,blo:30,blt:31,bso:32,bsc:33,bwo:34,bwt:35,bto:36,btr:37"/>
          <CheckBox x:Name="lha" Content="Has a hatch" dyl:Win.Column="27"/>
        </DockPanel>
        <DockPanel Style="{StaticResource Row}">
          <dyl:OpenButton x:Name="lbo" DockPanel.Dock="Right" ToolTip="Border Settings" dyl:Win.EnabledBy="lbr"
                          dyl:Win.Open="Dyl-QuickDrawBorderSettings.xaml"
                          dyl:Win.Columns="out:15,bco:17,bcv:18,blo:19,blt:20,bso:21,bsc:22,bwo:23,bwt:24,bto:25,btr:26"/>
          <CheckBox x:Name="lbr" Content="Has a border" dyl:Win.Column="14"/>
        </DockPanel>
      </StackPanel>
    </GroupBox>
    <!-- The assembly as it is drawn, a wall in plan, built as the layers are edited: -->
    <GroupBox Header="Preview" Margin="0,10,0,0">
      <dyl:AssemblyTile MinHeight="120" Radius="6" Rows="ll" Columns="0 1 2 5 7 8 9 14 6 16 27 38 39" Specs="lp/specs" Ends="ll/ends" Paper="ll/paper" BorderLines="abl" DividingLines="adl"
                        Ink="{DynamicResource Dyl.Text}" Fill="{DynamicResource Dyl.Input}" LabelBack="{DynamicResource Dyl.Surface}"
                        Accent="{DynamicResource Dyl.Accent}"/>
    </GroupBox>
    </DockPanel>

    <TextBlock x:Name="error" Grid.Row="2" Grid.ColumnSpan="5" Style="{DynamicResource Dyl.Error}" Margin="2,10,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap" Visibility="Collapsed"/>
    <!-- Reset: the default assemblies selected (or all of them) as the building code has them: -->
    <DockPanel Grid.Row="3" Grid.ColumnSpan="5" Margin="0,12,0,0">
      <Button x:Name="rst" DockPanel.Dock="Left" Margin="0" Content="Reset Selected"/>
      <Button x:Name="all" DockPanel.Dock="Left" Content="Reset All"/>
      <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" HorizontalAlignment="Right">
        <Button Content="OK" IsDefault="True"/>
        <Button Content="_Cancel" IsCancel="True"/>
        <Button x:Name="docs" Content="Open Docs"/>
      </StackPanel>
    </DockPanel>
  </Grid>
</Window>
